intent='EXPLAIN_ENTITY' resolved_entities=[] report='# Myocardial Infarction\n\nMyocardial Infarction, also known as MI, is a serious medical condition where blood flow to the heart muscle is blocked, causing damage to the heart muscle.\n\n### Causes\n\nMyocardial infarction is typically caused by a blockage in one or more of the coronary arteries, which supply blood to the heart muscle. This blockage can be caused by a blood clot or a narrowing of the coronary arteries due to atherosclerosis.\n\n### Symptoms\n\nSymptoms of myocardial infarction include chest pain, shortness of breath, lightheadedness, and cold sweat. Women may experience different symptoms, such as nausea, vomiting, or a feeling of indigestion.\n\n### Diagnosis\n\nDiagnosis of myocardial infarction typically involves a physical exam, medical history, and diagnostic tests such as an electrocardiogram (ECG) and a stress test.\n\n### Treatment\n\nTreatment for myocardial infarction typically involves medications to dissolve the blockage, such as thrombolytics, and/or a medical procedure to restore blood flow, such as angioplasty.\n\n### Prognosis\n\nPrognosis for myocardial infarction depends on the promptness and appropriateness of treatment.\n\n## Literature\n\nSeveral studies have investigated the effects of heavy metals on crop plants and the potential toxicity reduction strategies. For example, a study published in the International Journal of Phytoremediation found that certain heavy metals can be reduced in crop plants using a combination of phytoremediation and biochar. Another study published in the journal Advances in Biology found that oxidative stress-related features mined by weighted gene co-expression network analysis (WGCNA) and machine learning can predict respiratory syncytial virus infection.\n\nSources:\n\n* [1] Tiwari et al. (2026) Deciphering ways of heavy metals toxicity reduction in crop plants.\n* [2] Lei et al. (2026) Diagnostic Value of Oxidative Stress-Related Features Mined by WGCNA and Machine Learning in Respiratory Syncytial Virus Infection.\n* [3] Yu et al. (2026) Liquid-liquid phase separation and a phage-encoded inhibitor cooperatively drive transcriptional transition during phage SPO1 infection.\n* [4] Ganjoo et al. (2026) Myo-Inositol for Cutaneous Manifestations of Polycystic Ovary Syndrome: An International Delphi Consensus Recommendation for Dermatology Practice.\n* [5] Kharchuk et al. (2026) Characterization of poly-β-hydroxybutyrate and its biosynthesis in Priestia endophytica UCM B-5715.\n\nresolved entities:[{"canonical_name":"Myocardial Infarction","confidence":0.51,"description":"serious medical condition","entity_type":"Disease","identifier":"MESH:D009203","ontology":"MESH"}]'

